  >>> index_slices.indices.numpy()
  array([1, 3], dtype=int32)
  >>> index_slices.values.numpy()
  array([[1., 1., 1.],
         [1., 1., 1.]], dtype=float32)

  Contrast this representation with
  `tf.sparse.SparseTensor`,
  which uses multi-dimensional indices and scalar values.

